class Solution {
    public String reverseVowels(String s) {
        // Convert string to char array for easy swapping
        char[] chars = s.toCharArray();
        int left=0, right=chars.length - 1;
        while(left<right){
            while(left<right && !isVowel(chars[left])) left++; // Move left pointer until it finds a vowel
            while(left<right && !isVowel(chars[right])) right--; // Move right pointer until it finds a vowel
            
            // Swap vowels
            char temp=chars[left];
            chars[left]=chars[right];
            chars[right]=temp;

            left++;
            right--;
        }
        return new String(chars);
    }
    // Helper function to check if a character is a vowel
    private boolean isVowel(char c){
        return "aeiouAEIOU".indexOf(c)!=-1;
    }
}


Time Complexity: O(n) (each character checked once).
Space Complexity: O(n) for char array (but required since strings are immutable).
